[node name="CollisionUpper" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="."]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1.28, -2.5)
shape = SubResource("BoxUpper")

; THE COUPLING. No geometry of its own -- the plate meshes live under Body -- so this is a bare
; node running fifth_wheel.gd, at IDENTITY, with the kingpin marker as its child. TowHost reads
; `transform * marker.position`, so the datum below is still a chassis coordinate and the plate
; and the joint cannot disagree. The Drawbar / Pin shape (src/vehicles/tractor/drawbar.tscn).
[node name="FifthWheel" type="Node3D" parent="."]
script = ExtResource("3_fifthwheel")

; THE COUPLING DATUM, and y = 1.05 is SHARED GEOMETRY: every trailer in TrailerCatalog is
; authored with its ground at y = -1.05 against this plane, so a variant that raised or dropped
; it would float or bury all four. The Z is free per variant (0.45 here, 0.55 on the
; conventional) -- but the kingpin-to-rearmost-cab-structure gap is not; see test_truck. 0.45
; puts the plate 0.50 m ahead of the drive axle, which is where a real fifth wheel sits and what
; closes the gap between the cab and the trailer's nose to 0.70 m.
[node name="Kingpin" type="Marker3D" parent="FifthWheel"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 1.05, 0.45)

; THE VISUALS, and all of them are cosmetic EXCEPT ONE MEASUREMENT: `Cab`'s REAR FACE.
; test_truck and test_trailer read `Cab.position.z + mesh.size.z / 2` as the rearmost cab
; structure and pin the kingpin gap against the trailers' worst forward swing (1.50 m) plus a
; 0.30 m margin, so -1.40 is the furthest back anything here may reach. `Cab` must therefore
; stay a MeshInstance3D with a BoxMesh under this name; the rest of its size is free, and the
; roof fairing stops at -1.45 to stay ahead of it rather than relying on the test not looking.
; The cab's own drag area comes off the COLLISION box, not these meshes, so reshaping the
; shell does not re-derive semi_spec.tres.
;
; The nose is narrower than the flanks (+-0.86 against +-0.96) with a 21 deg corner panel
; bridging them. That taper is the silhouette: a cab-over with parallel sides reads as a crate.
;
; TWO BOXES THAT TOUCH ON A FACE PLANE Z-FIGHT; two that overlap never do. Every axis-aligned
; BoxMesh pair here is swept by test_trailer.gd's test_no_two_boxes_share_a_face_plane_and_a_facing
; on all three axes, so a new detail part goes 1-3 cm proud or inset rather than flush. Parts
; that are ROTATED (the corner panels, fairing, visor, screen, arch quarters, bumper ends) are
; outside that sweep by construction, and so are the visor's markers, which are its children.
[node name="Body" type="Node3D" parent="."]

